## What this verifies

<a DEPLOYED environment is up and serving — fast, read-only, safe against production.>

## How it runs

1. `build/stages/60-verify.sh` runs `smoke.md` right after `./build/deploy`
   lands. Read the target from `ENVIRONMENT`, `DEPLOY_TO`, `DEPLOY_TAG`.
2. Read-only and idempotent: it runs against production.
3. Required before any prod release — the deploy is refused without a
   `smoke.md` that lists at least one test.

`run_command` runs from the project root and must exit non-zero on failure.
Run it by hand once before adding it to the suite.

